     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"DE-CH\" link=\"#467886\" vlink=\"#96607D\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Dear all,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Michael Schaub and I have started working on a 2<sup>nd</sup> edition of the Bayesian Population Analysis, or BPA, book. We were wondering\r\n whether we want to have exercises again. For this we would like to ask this:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:normal\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Among those who own either the first edition of the BPA book or the IPM book, what approximate percentage of the exercises have\r\n you tried to solve ?<u></u><u></u></span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Thanks and best regards  ---  M &amp; M<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
    ]
   ]
